<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport"
          content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Password Strength Guide</title>
</head>

<body>

<header>

    <h1>🔐 Password Strength Guide</h1>

    <p>
        Learn basic principles for creating stronger passwords.
    </p>

</header>

<hr>

<main>

<section>

    <h2>🛡️ Password Checklist</h2>

    <ul>

        <li>Use a long password.</li>

        <li>Avoid easily guessed personal information.</li>

        <li>Use different passwords for important accounts.</li>

        <li>Consider using a reputable password manager.</li>

        <li>Enable multi-factor authentication when available.</li>

    </ul>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>📊 Example Strength Levels</h2>

    <table border="1" cellpadding="10">

        <tr>
            <th>Level</th>
            <th>General Description</th>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Weak</td>
            <td>Short or easy to guess</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Moderate</td>
            <td>Longer but predictable</td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>Strong</td>
            <td>Long and difficult to guess</td>
        </tr>

    </table>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>💡 Why Password Length Matters</h2>

    <p>
        Longer passwords generally provide more possible
        combinations, making guessing more difficult.
    </p>

</section>

<hr>

<section>

    <h2>❓ Security Tip</h2>

    <details>

        <summary>
            Should you share your password?
        </summary>

        <p>
            No. Keep passwords private and never share
            them through messages or public websites.
        </p>

    </details>

</section>

</main>

<footer>

    <hr>

    <p>
        Password Security Guide — Educational Project
    </p>

</footer>

</body>
</html>
